# SRD PDF source (SRD_CC_v5.2.1)

When building or changing SRD parsers, consolidation scripts, or `data/srd/` assets:

## Local source file

- **Path:** `data/srd-source/SRD_CC_v5.2.1.pdf`
- Treat this PDF as ground truth for **section structure**, page counts, and heading boundaries.
- Attach in chat with `@data/srd-source/SRD_CC_v5.2.1.pdf` when scoping parser work.

## Required workflow before changing taxonomy

1. Run dry-run extraction and read counts/logs:
   ```bash
   npm run build:macro-srd -- --dry-run
   npm run parse:srd-pdf -- --dry-run
   ```
2. Compare PDF-derived boundaries to bundled index (`srdDocumentIndex.data.ts`).
3. Prefer **header-based** boundaries (`#` / `##` titles), not page breaks.

## Source priority

| Priority | Source | Use for |
|----------|--------|---------|
| 1 | PDF stream | Structure validation, streaming parser logic, page metadata |
| 2 | Bundled markdown (`srdDocument.data.ts`) | Full-fidelity text, tables, nested headings when PDF columns garble text |
| 3 | Hybrid (`parse:srd-pdf` default) | PDF scan + markdown backfill when yields are low |

## Output constraints

- Do **not** truncate descriptions, tables, or glossary text in JSON outputs.
- Retain metadata on every record: `_source_file`, `start`/`end`, `pagePrefix` (or `<!-- page:N -->` from PDF stream).
- Macro-scoped outputs live in `data/srd/macro/`; unified DB in `data/srd/srd_database.json`.

## Commands

```bash
npm run build:macro-srd -- --dry-run
npm run build:macro-srd
npm run parse:srd-pdf -- --dry-run
npm run parse:srd-pdf
npm run consolidate:srd-macro -- --dry-run
```

Default `--pdf` path is `data/srd-source/SRD_CC_v5.2.1.pdf` — no path override needed when the file is present.
